# Grid B — U5 Test coverage (negative enumeration)
#
# Gap target: test-coverage answers require enumerating functions
# WITHOUT matching _test.go counterparts — no scenario for
# "absence" enumeration, no evidence kind for test artifacts. This
# case measures whether the pipeline can reach that differential
# answer.
#
# Ground truth: subject to drift (tests are added over time). The
# case leans on EXPECT_CONTAINS="compiler" to establish scope and
# negative anchors to block lazy "all covered" answers. Absolute
# correctness requires manual inspection — this case's value is in
# forcing the shape, not pinning the list.
#
# Anti-hallucination: "no gaps / fully covered" is dispositive of
# the LLM not having actually read compile.go + templates.go.
ID="u5a"
NAME="test coverage — uncovered exported functions in compiler package"
QUESTION="internal/analysis/compiler 包里哪些导出函数（首字母大写）目前没有对应的 _test.go 测试覆盖？逐一列出函数名。"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC was just `compiler` (the
# package name in the question) — bar = "复述题目". Tighten by
# requiring the answer to name AT LEAST ONE specific exported
# function (`Compile` / `RecomputeBudget` / `InferScenario` are the
# 3 canonical exports per `grep '^func [A-Z]' internal/analysis/
# compiler/*.go`). The list of which are uncovered drifts as tests
# are added; the bar is "answer surfaces a real exported function
# name", not "answer matches a fixed list". Honest "all covered"
# answers must justify with the same function names; this gate
# distinguishes investigation from hand-wavy.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="compiler"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="\b(Compile|RecomputeBudget|InferScenario|Output|BuildOutput)\b"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="all.covered no.gaps fully.tested"
